repository-code: >-
  https://github.com/pedroartelabs/pedroarte-labs-sdd-spdd-ia-first-patterns
url: >-
  https://github.com/pedroartelabs/pedroarte-labs-sdd-spdd-ia-first-patterns
abstract: >-
  A public reference implementation of governed AI-First software delivery. It
  combines Spec-Driven Development (SDD), Structured Prompt-Driven Development
  (SPDD) using the REASONS model, Hexagonal Architecture organised by bounded
  context, executable architecture fitness functions, Claude Code Skills,
  subagents and enforcement hooks, and deterministic CI quality gates, with
  working reference implementations in Java and Python. Its central claim is
  that in an AI-First process artificial intelligence must be a governed
  participant in the engineering cycle rather than an unconstrained code
  generator, and that architectural rules are only real when something
  automated enforces them — demonstrated here by deliberately invalid fixtures
  that the controls are proven to reject.
